  "worked_solution": "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nu=6i-2j,\\,a=-i+4j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $t=3\\,\\text{h},$ the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(6i-2j)+(-i+4j)(3) \\\\  & =(6i-2j)+(-3i+12j) \\\\  & =(3\\,i+10\\,j)\\,\\text{km/h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v| & =|3i+10j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{10}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+100} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{109}\\,\\text{km/h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
